# SS-23 - Agent-accessible simulation lab and teaching skill
Workstream ID: SS-23
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/23
Status: DONE
Milestone: M2
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-04, SS-06, SS-21

## Purpose
Enable agents and humans to fetch real observations, test hypothetical capital,
explain algorithms and evaluate new hypotheses through a reusable detailed skill
and a headless, provenance-preserving interface.

## Tasks
- [x] Add JSON catalogue, actual history fetch and recorded-input simulation commands.
- [x] Reuse the common next-open accounting engine for built-in/custom targets.
- [x] Add bounded declarative custom rules without eval/code execution.
- [x] Write a detailed repository skill, exact commands and usable custom examples.
- [x] Verify independent arithmetic, causality, error paths and actual provider execution.
- [x] Document results, operating instructions and boundaries.

## Acceptance criteria
- Supplied capital, fees, dates and rules are captured exactly with marked INR/% results.
- Full observations, targets, fills, curves, provenance, custom rule and input hashes persist.
- Outputs refuse overwrite; invalid data/rules fail explicitly without substitute prices.
- Custom rules reject future offsets/code, unsupported features and ambiguous entry/exit.
- Skill teaches losses, uncertainty, drawdown, holdouts, learning explanations and limits;
  it does not promise profits, fabricate owner mastery or authorize orders.
- Other agents can read the skill and invoke the headless interface without a GUI.

## Completion evidence
- Full offline suite: 322 passed, 4 opt-in live cases skipped, normal exit;
  Ruff lint/format, strict mypy and Git whitespace checks passed.
- Actual headless ICICIBANK fetch returned 496 observations through 2026-11-20.
  All 27 built-ins ran on the same captured data and hypothetical INR 100,000;
  15 returned a marked profit and 12 a loss. Neither result category was hidden.
- Both shipped custom examples matched corresponding built-in targets, fills
  and equity. The documented actual custom-rule command returned a saved receipt.
- Detailed skill was discovered enabled as a project skill and, after registering
  the canonical directory, as a custom skill from outside this checkout.
  Its current-fundamental Python example also ran on the saved actual bank snapshot.
- Invalid/ambiguous inputs and provider failures return explicit errors; immutable
  outputs preserve actual observations, costs, rules, decisions/fills and hashes.
- No embedded LLM, orders, automatic optimisation, new EXE, human learning
  acceptance or independent profitability proof is implied.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-21: User requested agent/human operation, hypothetical capital,
  agent-authored algorithms and LLM-assisted explanations. Added a versioned
  repository skill and bounded data-only rule language, not an arbitrary plugin runner.
- 2026-11-21: Completed the shared-engine headless interface, skill/examples,
  actual built-in/custom experiments and validation. No dependency installation
  or global duplicate skill copy; other agent hosts can load the same Markdown.
